(5514388, 788047, 68546, '<td valign="top">Very nice clean portrait, the lighting is good and nicely filled to soften the shadows. I would usually try to meet the tip of the nose shadow with the cheekbone shadow if using this lighting pattern, especially seen as it''s most of the way across the top lip but that''s a relatively minor thing. The colours work really well and it has a lot of depth and clarity to it. It''s a slightly odd crop with it grazing the arm on the right and it''s not a wow shot but a very nice clean portrait. Well done</td>', 'Very nice clean portrait, the lighting is good and nicely filled to soften the shadows. I would usually try to meet the tip of the nose shadow with the cheekbone shadow if using this lighting pattern, especially seen as it''s most of the way across the top lip but that''s a relatively minor thing. The colours work really well and it has a lot of depth and clarity to it. It''s a slightly odd crop with it grazing the arm on the right and it''s not a wow shot but a very nice clean portrait. Well done', '2009-06-04 16:48:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5514392, 793581, 68546, '<td valign="top">wow what a scene! beautiful lighting through the clouds highlighting the mountain. I''m not sure I''m too keen on the viewpoint or composition though. The path is great for a lead in line and the rocks to the right frame the mountain nicely but it feels like these were included for this reason rather then to enhance the composition. I think this makes the mountain a small part of the picture when I''m seeing it as the focal point. To me the path is too promanant and is actually leading me out of the frame on the left rather then into the mountain. A great scene though and well captured, I''m just not sure it''s the best framing? Hope that makes sense.</td>', 'wow what a scene! beautiful lighting through the clouds highlighting the mountain. I''m not sure I''m too keen on the viewpoint or composition though. The path is great for a lead in line and the rocks to the right frame the mountain nicely but it feels like these were included for this reason rather then to enhance the composition. I think this makes the mountain a small part of the picture when I''m seeing it as the focal point. To me the path is too promanant and is actually leading me out of the frame on the left rather then into the mountain. A great scene though and well captured, I''m just not sure it''s the best framing? Hope that makes sense.', '2009-06-04 16:52:30.000000', NULL, 1),
